The source code in this repository is public so that it can be read, but it is
not licensed for reuse: no permission is given to copy, modify, distribute or
use it, in whole or in part, without written permission from the copyright
holder (support@pistemtl.ca).

Third-party code keeps its own licences. The libraries in prototypes/vendor/
(MapLibre GL JS, under the BSD 3-Clause licence, and PMTiles, under the BSD
3-Clause licence) are not covered by the notice above; their licence texts are
in prototypes/vendor/maplibre/LICENSE.txt and prototypes/vendor/pmtiles/LICENSE.txt.

Data keeps its own licences, and each source must be credited as it asks. This
notice does not cover it. The sources the app uses, and their licences:

  - Ville de Montréal open data (bike network, streets, speed limits, works,
    parks and others): Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 (CC BY 4.0).
  - OpenStreetMap contributors (paths off the island, places, building
    footprints): Open Database Licence (ODbL).
  - OpenFreeMap and OpenMapTiles (the base map): the OpenStreetMap licence above,
    with OpenMapTiles' own attribution.
  - NRCan HRDEM and the CMM 2023 and 2024 LiDAR terrain and building heights:
    Open Government Licence - Canada.
  - AWS Terrain Tiles (elevation beyond our own terrain tiles): public dataset,
    under its own terms.
  - STM GTFS (metro lines and stations): STM's open data terms.
  - BIXI GBFS (station locations and live status): BIXI's open data terms.
  - Open-Meteo (weather forecast): CC BY 4.0, free for non-commercial use.
  - Environment and Climate Change Canada (rain radar, through GeoMet): Open
    Government Licence - Canada.
  - Wikimedia Commons photos of the classic rides: their authors' free licences
    (CC BY and CC BY-SA), credited on each card and listed in
    prototypes/shared/photos/credits.json.

The full list and the notes on each source are in docs/03_data_sources.md.
